From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] Keep Vulkan handles whole in 32-bit builds

A non-dispatchable handle is a uint64_t in a 32-bit build, so the series'
casts through uintptr_t dropped its upper half: a guest-assigned handle lost
its process tag, and the guest's caches keyed handles by their lower half.
The casts become caboose::handle_key and caboose::to_handle
(../bounded-memory/handles.h), which are the same casts in a 64-bit build.

